<div class="features-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Why P2P Model Delivery?</h2>
    <div class="problem-card">
        <p>AI models are <strong>big</strong> — 100MB to 2GB+. CDNs can't scale when every user downloads the same model.
        SpawnDev.WebTorrent turns every browser into a peer. The more users, the faster delivery.
        HuggingFace serves the model <em>once</em> — the swarm handles the rest.</p>
    </div>

    <h2 class="section-title" style="margin-top: 3rem;">Architecture</h2>

    <div class="features-grid features-grid-3">
        <div class="feature-card feature-highlight-p2p">
            <div class="feature-icon">&#x1F517;</div>
            <h3>Pure C# Client</h3>
            <p>Full BitTorrent wire protocol, piece management, SHA-1 verification, WebRTC transport for browser peers, TCP for desktop. No JavaScript dependencies.</p>
            <div class="feature-tag">SpawnDev.WebTorrent</div>
        </div>
        <div class="feature-card feature-highlight-p2p">
            <div class="feature-icon">&#x1F4E1;</div>
            <h3>Tracker + Web Seed Server</h3>
            <p>WebSocket tracker with WebRTC signaling relay. HTTP range request web seed (BEP 17/19). Reusable library — use it without HuggingFace.</p>
            <div class="feature-tag">SpawnDev.WebTorrent.Server</div>
        </div>
        <div class="feature-card feature-highlight-p2p">
            <div class="feature-icon">&#x1F917;</div>
            <h3>HuggingFace Proxy</h3>
            <p>Fetches model files from HuggingFace CDN, caches locally, generates .torrent files on demand, serves as web seed. Optional extension.</p>
            <div class="feature-tag">SpawnDev.WebTorrent.Server.HuggingFace</div>
        </div>
    </div>

    <h2 class="section-title" style="margin-top: 3rem;">Key Features</h2>

    <div class="features-grid features-grid-3">
        <div class="feature-card">
            <div class="feature-icon">&#x1F3AF;</div>
            <h3>Random-Access Streaming</h3>
            <p>Read any byte range from a torrent file as it downloads. Perfect for ML weight loading — stream weights directly to GPU.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="feature-card">
            <div class="feature-icon">&#x1F4BE;</div>
            <h3>Persistent Caching</h3>
            <p>Downloaded pieces persist in OPFS (browser) or filesystem (desktop). Models load instantly on return visits.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="feature-card">
            <div class="feature-icon">&#x1F6E1;</div>
            <h3>Piece Verification</h3>
            <p>Every piece is SHA-1/SHA-256 verified against the .torrent manifest. Corrupted data is rejected and re-requested automatically.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="feature-card">
            <div class="feature-icon">&#x26A1;</div>
            <h3>Zero Config</h3>
            <p>ModelTorrentClient handles everything: .torrent fetch, piece download, verification, assembly. One line to download a model.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="feature-card">
            <div class="feature-icon">&#x1F30D;</div>
            <h3>Desktop + Browser</h3>
            <p>Same library runs on .NET console/desktop apps and Blazor WebAssembly. TCP transport for desktop, WebRTC for browser.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="feature-card">
            <div class="feature-icon">&#x1F4CA;</div>
            <h3>Bandwidth Respectful</h3>
            <p>Configurable upload limits. Conservative defaults. Users choose how much they contribute. Nobody gets a surprise bandwidth bill.</p>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>

<div class="code-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Quick Start</h2>

    <div class="steps-container">
        <div class="step">
            <div class="step-number">1</div>
            <div class="step-content">
                <h3>Download a Model</h3>
                <p>One line to download any HuggingFace model via the torrent network.</p>
                <div class="code-block">
                    <pre><code><span class="keyword">var</span> client = <span class="keyword">new</span> <span class="type">ModelTorrentClient</span>(<span class="keyword">new</span> <span class="type">ModelTorrentOptions</span>
{
    ServerBaseUrl = <span class="string">"https://hub.spawndev.com:44365"</span>
});

<span class="keyword">var</span> weights = <span class="keyword">await</span> client.<span class="method">DownloadModelAsync</span>(
    <span class="string">"Xenova/distilgpt2"</span>, <span class="string">"onnx/model.onnx"</span>);</code></pre>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="step">
            <div class="step-number">2</div>
            <div class="step-content">
                <h3>Stream with Random Access</h3>
                <p>Read any byte range — pieces download on demand as you read.</p>
                <div class="code-block">
                    <pre><code><span class="keyword">var</span> stream = <span class="keyword">await</span> client.<span class="method">GetModelStreamAsync</span>(
    <span class="string">"Xenova/distilgpt2"</span>, <span class="string">"onnx/model.onnx"</span>);

<span class="comment">// Read 64KB from offset 1MB — only those pieces download</span>
<span class="keyword">var</span> chunk = <span class="keyword">await</span> stream.<span class="method">ReadAsync</span>(offset: <span class="number">1_000_000</span>, length: <span class="number">65536</span>);</code></pre>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="step">
            <div class="step-number">3</div>
            <div class="step-content">
                <h3>Run Your Own Server</h3>
                <p>Tracker + web seed + HuggingFace proxy in a few lines.</p>
                <div class="code-block">
                    <pre><code><span class="keyword">var</span> tracker = <span class="keyword">new</span> <span class="type">TorrentTracker</span>();
<span class="keyword">var</span> proxy = <span class="keyword">new</span> <span class="type">HuggingFaceProxy</span>();

app.<span class="method">MapWebTorrentServer</span>(tracker);
app.<span class="method">MapHuggingFaceProxy</span>(proxy);

<span class="comment">// Clients download from peers first, fall back to your cached HF data</span></code></pre>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>

<div class="vision-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">The Vision</h2>
    <div class="vision-grid">
        <div class="vision-card">
            <div class="vision-icon">&#x1F310;</div>
            <h3>Swarm Training</h3>
            <p>10,000 consumer GPUs donating idle cycles. TurboQuant-compressed gradients flowing through the DHT. Ed25519-signed updates via BEP 46. The volunteer supercomputer for AI — Folding@@Home for neural networks.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="vision-card">
            <div class="vision-icon">&#x1F9E0;</div>
            <h3>AcceleratorType.P2P</h3>
            <p>A 7th <a href="https://github.com/LostBeard/SpawnDev.ILGPU" style="color:#a78bfa">SpawnDev.ILGPU</a> backend that distributes kernels across connected devices via <code>SwarmCompute</code>. Same C# kernel code runs on 1 GPU or 10,000 GPUs. Transparently.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="vision-card">
            <div class="vision-icon">&#x1F91D;</div>
            <h3>AI Agent Shared Memory</h3>
            <p>BEP 46 DHT mutable items + <code>AgentChannel</code> pub/sub. Agents share KV cache, model weights, and coordination state via the BitTorrent DHT. No server. WebCrypto-signed. Browser-native.</p>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>

